  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Using the trapezoidal rule with the partition\n\n$$\n[-1,2]=[-1,0]\\cup [0,2],\n$$\n\napproximate the area under the curve of the function $y=\\frac{10}{1+{x}^{2}}.$",
  "worked_solution": "Let $f(x)=\\frac{10}{1+{x}^{2}}.$ Let's plot this function:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067661/assets/c4c9aa8e615747199462e0597f4cb7be82031efdb5b2f6585e3fb9c0b652ee78.png)\n\nWe've drawn some trapezoids to help calculate our trapezoidal rule sum. By calculating the area of each trapezoid, we obtain the following approximation for our area $A:$\n\n$$\nA\u2248\\overset{1\\text{st trapezoid}}{\\overset{\u23de}{[\\,\\frac{\\overset{\\text{bases}}{\\overset{\u23de}{f(-1)+f(0)}}}{2}\\,\\cdot \\,{{\u0394{x}_{1}}_{\u23df}}_{\\text{height}}\\,]}}+\\overset{2\\text{nd trapezoid}}{\\overset{\u23de}{[\\,\\frac{\\overset{\\text{bases}}{\\overset{\u23de}{f(0)+f(2)}}}{2}\\,\\cdot \\,{{\u0394{x}_{2}}_{\u23df}}_{\\text{height}}\\,]}}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the appropriate numbers into the above expression gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & \u2248\\frac{5+10}{2}\\cdot (0-(-1))+\\frac{10+2}{2}\\cdot (2-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{2}\\cdot 1+\\frac{12}{2}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{2}+12 \\\\  & =\\frac{39}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
